My own read as art director (looked at the overview sheet; opinion, not score):
  - Fireball is the strongest family: all five read as one world. d4 (dying
    star) and d2 (burning rock) are my picks.
  - Planet: d1 (banded) and d4 (inside out, orange fissures) are the most
    readable at 1x. d3's swirl sits close to the coin's galaxy look.
  - Meteorite: d2 (iron), d4 (pumice) and d6 (chondrite) give a good
    random pool together. d3 (frost) reads a little like a snowcap.
  - UFO: d1 and d4 are clean; d2 (wrecked) is busy at 1x and is the one
    shrunk to 90% (open item 3).
  - Electric ball: d2 reads as electricity; d4's swirl leans toward the
    coin's galaxy, which risks the "solid fuchsia = coin" read (rule 6).
  - Coin d1 vs d2: close; d2's rare frame stands out more.

